  "step_3": "The decision reason hinges on the presence or absence of a sure (i.e., 100% probable) outcome in each lottery. However, neither lottery contains a sure outcome, so the reason cannot clearly prefer one over the other. The individual does not refer to or consider whether any outcome is certain (i.e., 100% likely), which would be necessary to apply this reason. Instead, they focus on the relative probabilities of winning something and prefer the lottery with the higher chance of a non-zero outcome. This reasoning aligns more with a 'maximize chance of winning' heuristic than with evaluating the presence of a sure outcome. There is no indication that the individual assessed whether either lottery offered a guaranteed result. Therefore, the relevant information from the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome) was not considered, and the justification does not match the rule of the reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
